@openuidev/lang-core 0.2.18: telemetry off.

The parser and the prompt generator post sampled usage events to PostHog when the runtime opts in
(OPENUI_RUNTIME_TELEMETRY_ENABLED in a Node process environment); the event reads git's origin through
node:child_process (execFile) and the ci-info package. Moqui never sends them: postCapture, the two send and capture
functions of each event, recordSystemPromptGeneration, prepareParserParseTelemetry, readGitOrigin,
getRepositoryIdentifier and getProjectHash are emptied (they return at once), and getCIInfo no longer imports ci-info,
so the bundle has no network call, no process call and no dynamic import (refresh.mjs checks the bundle for them).
Reviewed Oct 22, 2026. Applied by libs/refresh.mjs to dist/index.mjs of the npm package before the bundle is built.

